{"id":"048af8ca986135e46ab0e68e802c33d3808d3496","url":"https://vcarl.com/sashay","title":"Sashay: sliding panes for the web","site_name":"Zeli","source":"Hacker News · 24h最热","byline":null,"excerpt":"A sliding-panes layout for the web. Snaps, flings, bottom bars, deep stacks, and a layout that fits in a URL.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><DIV><section aria-label=\"Live demo\"><astro-island uid=\"ZRweMO\" prefix=\"r3\" component-url=\"/sashay/_astro/Hero.BYDHcMuZ.js\" component-export=\"Hero\" renderer-url=\"/sashay/_astro/client.Cd-EeyjT.js\" props=\"{&quot;base&quot;:[0,&quot;/sashay/&quot;]}\" ssr=\"\" client=\"load\" opts=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hero&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:true}\" await-children=\"\"><div id=\"hero\" data-sashay-frame=\"\" data-sashay-ssr=\"_r3R_1_\"><div aria-label=\"Hello\" data-sashay-pane=\"hello\"><div><p>Drag the edge between two panes to resize them. The edge settles at a simple fraction of the width, and a pane with no room left slides under its neighbour. The layout can be saved in the URL.</p></div><div> <p><span>This headline is a pane. Grab the edge to its right.</span><span>This headline is a pane. On a phone the edges become tabs: tap one.</span></p></div></div><div data-sashay-pane=\"why\" aria-label=\"Why\"><h2>Why panes?</h2><p>Power users want to arrange their screen the way they work. Panes give them that without making the interface complicated: each pane is an ordinary view, and the only new control is the edge between them.</p><p>That makes them a good middle ground between a fully customisable UI, where any panel can go anywhere, and a simple responsive layout that decides everything for you.</p></div><div data-sashay-pane=\"install\" data-bar=\"\" aria-label=\"Install\"><h2>Hang it in a frame.</h2><pre><span>// @vcarl/sashay/react</span>\n&lt;Sashay\n  onLayoutChange={save}&gt;\n  &lt;Pane id=<span>\"list\"</span>\n    title=<span>\"List\"</span>\n    focus={<span>1/3</span>}&gt;…&lt;/Pane&gt;\n  &lt;Pane id=<span>\"detail\"</span>\n    title=<span>\"Detail\"</span>\n    focus={<span>1/2</span>}&gt;…&lt;/Pane&gt;\n&lt;/Sashay&gt;</pre></div><div data-sashay-bar=\"install\"><p><span>ESM only</span><span>React ≥19</span><span>0-dep core</span><span>MIT</span></p></div></div><p><span><span>?layout=</span><span>69.0</span></span><span>This code is the layout. Drag an edge, throw it, or click one to open and close.</span></p><!--astro:end--></astro-island></section><section aria-label=\"Features\"><div><h2>Snaps to simple fractions.</h2><p>Dividers rest on fractions with a denominator up to six, so a layout saved on a laptop still makes sense on a monitor. The grid gets finer as the frame gets wider.</p><p><a data-cta=\"cell_snaps\" href=\"/sashay/guide/#your-first-frame\">Guide: Your first frame →</a></p></div><div><h2>Throw it.</h2><p>A quick throw carries the divider one or two snaps past where you let go. Release speed is read from the last 90&#160;ms, so a slow drag still lands exactly where you put it.</p><p><a data-cta=\"cell_throw\" href=\"/sashay/guide/#your-first-frame\">Guide: Your first frame →</a></p></div><div><h2>A bar for each pane.</h2><p>Any pane can have a bar at its bottom for filters, settings or a table of contents. It expands over the pane and works the same on a phone.</p><p><a data-cta=\"cell_bar\" href=\"/sashay/guide/#bottom-bars\">Guide: Bottom bars →</a></p><div id=\"cell-bar\"><p><label> Open</label><label> Mine</label><label> Archived</label></p></div></div><div><h2>Deep stacks fold into a spine.</h2><p>Drill down as far as you like. Panes that no longer fit fold into a slim spine, with a tab for each. Drag cost stays flat at a thousand deep.</p><p><a data-cta=\"cell_spine\" href=\"/sashay/guide/#navigation-stacks\">Guide: Navigation stacks →</a></p><div id=\"cell-spine\"><div data-sashay-pane=\"s1\"><p><b>1</b></p></div><div data-sashay-pane=\"s2\"><p><b>2</b></p></div></div></div><div><h2>Deep linked pane arrangements</h2><p>Which panes are open, how wide they are, and which bars are open all fit in a short code you can keep in the URL. Share the link and the other person sees the same arrangement.</p><p><a data-cta=\"cell_layout_code\" href=\"/sashay/guide/#layout-in-the-url\">Guide: Layout in the URL →</a></p></div></section><section aria-labelledby=\"seeit-h\"><h2 id=\"seeit-h\">See it work.</h2><figure><div><astro-island uid=\"ZhU9Xx\" prefix=\"r4\" component-url=\"/sashay/_astro/browser.CbHPj9_-.js\" component-export=\"PlantsDemo\" renderer-url=\"/sashay/_astro/client.Cd-EeyjT.js\" props=\"{&quot;compactBelow&quot;:[0,&quot;30rem&quot;]}\" ssr=\"\" client=\"load\" opts=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;PlantsDemo&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:true}\" await-children=\"\"><div data-sashay-frame=\"\" data-sashay-ssr=\"_r4R_2_\"><section data-sashay-pane=\"chart\" data-bar=\"\" aria-label=\"Chart\"><h3>Houseplants</h3><p>Sun against water. Pick a plant.</p><svg width=\"720\" height=\"440\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Houseplants by sun and water\"><g><line x1=\"44\" x2=\"44\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"16\" /><text x=\"44\" y=\"418\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text></g><g><line x1=\"174.4\" x2=\"174.4\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"16\" /><text x=\"174.4\" y=\"418\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text></g><g><line x1=\"304.8\" x2=\"304.8\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"16\" /><text x=\"304.8\" y=\"418\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text></g><g><line x1=\"435.2\" x2=\"435.2\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"16\" /><text x=\"435.2\" y=\"418\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text></g><g><line x1=\"565.6\" x2=\"565.6\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"16\" /><text x=\"565.6\" y=\"418\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text></g><g><line x1=\"696\" x2=\"696\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"16\" /><text x=\"696\" y=\"418\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text></g><g><line x1=\"44\" x2=\"696\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"400\" /><text x=\"34\" y=\"404\" text-anchor=\"end\">0</text></g><g><line x1=\"44\" x2=\"696\" y1=\"304\" y2=\"304\" /><text x=\"34\" y=\"308\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text></g><g><line x1=\"44\" x2=\"696\" 