the chart and your plant stays in view.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<h3>The house</h3>","sentences":[{"en":"The house","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>6 things</p>","sentences":[{"en":"6 things","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<h3>Parlour</h3>","sentences":[{"en":"Parlour","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>2 things</p>","sentences":[{"en":"2 things","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<figcaption><b>A house, all the way down.</b> Rooms, dressers, drawers, a tin box. The old levels fold into the spine.</figcaption>","sentences":[{"en":"A house, all the way down.","zh":null},{"en":"Rooms, dressers, drawers, a tin box.","zh":null},{"en":"The old levels fold into the spine.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><b>0</b><span>runtime dependencies</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"0runtime dependencies","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><b>&lt;2ms</b><span>drag frame at 1,000 panes</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"<2msdrag frame at 1,000 panes","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><b>← →</b><span>keyboard on every edge, aria-valuenow</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"← →keyboard on every edge, aria-valuenow","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><b>1.3.1</b><span>React ≥19, or the vanilla core · MIT</span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"1.3.1React ≥19, or the vanilla core · MIT","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><b>sashay</b> &#160;·&#160; a sash window is made of sliding panes.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"sashay · a sash window is made of sliding panes.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>This site counts visits, clicks and demo use with PostHog, without cookies.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"This site counts visits, clicks and demo use with PostHog, without cookies.","zh":null}]}],"translated":true,"content_html_zh":"<div class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div><section aria-label=\"Live demo\"><astro-island uid=\"ZRweMO\" prefix=\"r3\" component-url=\"/sashay/_astro/Hero.BYDHcMuZ.js\" component-export=\"Hero\" renderer-url=\"/sashay/_astro/client.Cd-EeyjT.js\" props=\"{&quot;base&quot;:[0,&quot;/sashay/&quot;]}\" ssr=\"\" client=\"load\" opts=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hero&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:true}\" await-children=\"\"><div id=\"hero\" data-sashay-frame=\"\" data-sashay-ssr=\"_r3R_1_\"><div aria-label=\"Hello\" data-sashay-pane=\"hello\"><div><p>Drag the edge between two panes to resize them. The edge settles at a simple fraction of the width, and a pane with no room left slides under its neighbour. The layout can be saved in the URL.</p></div><div> <p>This headline is a pane. Grab the edge to its right.This headline is a pane. On a phone the edges become tabs: tap one.</p></div></div><div data-sashay-pane=\"why\" aria-label=\"Why\"><h2>Why panes?</h2><p>Power users want to arrange their screen the way they work. Panes give them that without making the interface complicated: each pane is an ordinary view, and the only new control is the edge between them.</p><p>That makes them a good middle ground between a fully customisable UI, where any panel can go anywhere, and a simple responsive layout that decides everything for you.</p></div><div data-sashay-pane=\"install\" data-bar=\"\" aria-label=\"Install\"><h2>Hang it in a frame.</h2><pre><span>// @vcarl/sashay/react</span>\n&lt;Sashay\n  onLayoutChange={save}&gt;\n  &lt;Pane id=<span>\"list\"</span>\n    title=<span>\"List\"</span>\n    focus={<span>1/3</span>}&gt;…&lt;/Pane&gt;\n  &lt;Pane id=<span>\"detail\"</span>\n    title=<span>\"Detail\"</span>\n    focus={<span>1/2</span>}&gt;…&lt;/Pane&gt;\n&lt;/Sashay&gt;</pre></div><div data-sashay-bar=\"install\"><p>ESM onlyReact ≥190-dep coreMIT</p></div></div><p>?layout=69.0This code is the layout. Drag an edge, throw it, or click one to open and close.</p><!--astro:end--></astro-island></section><section aria-label=\"Features\"><div><h2>Snaps to simple fractions.</h2><p>Dividers rest on fractions with a denominator up to six, so a layout saved on a laptop still makes sense on a monitor. The grid gets finer as the frame gets wider.</p><p>Guide: Your first frame →</p></div><div><h2>Throw it.</h2><p>A quick throw carries the divider one or two snaps past where you let go. Release speed is read from the last 90 ms, so a slow drag still lands exactly where you put it.</p><p>Guide: Your first frame →</p></div><div><h2>A bar for each pane.</h2><p>Any pane can have a bar at its bottom for filters, settings or a table of contents. It expands over the pane and works the same on a phone.</p><p>Guide: Bottom bars →</p><div id=\"cell-bar\"><p>Open Mine Archived</p></div></div><div><h2>Deep stacks fold into a spine.</h2><p>Drill down as far as you like. Panes that no longer fit fold into a slim spine, with a tab for each. Drag cost stays flat at a thousand deep.</p><p>Guide: Navigation stacks →</p><div id=\"cell-spine\"><div data-sashay-pane=\"s1\"><p><b>1</b></p></div><div data-sashay-pane=\"s2\"><p><b>2</b></p></div></div></div><div><h2>Deep linked pane arrangements</h2><p>Which panes are open, how wide they are, and which bars are open all fit in a short code you can keep in the URL. Share the link and the other person sees the same arrangement.</p><p>Guide: Layout in the URL →</p></div></section><section aria-labelledby=\"seeit-h\"><h2 id=\"seeit-h\">看到它起作用了。</h2><figure><div><astro-island uid=\"ZhU9Xx\" prefix=\"r4\" component-url=\"/sashay/_astro/browser.CbHPj9_-.js\" component-export=\"PlantsDemo\" renderer-url=\"/sashay/_astro/client.Cd-EeyjT.js\" props=\"{&quot;compactBelow&quot;:[0,&quot;30rem&quot;]}\" ssr=\"\" client=\"load\" opts=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;PlantsDemo&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:true}\" await-children=\"\"><div data-sashay-frame=\"\" data-sashay-ssr=\"_r4R_2_\"><section data-sashay-pane=\"chart\" data-bar=\"\" aria-label=\"Chart\"><h3>Houseplants</h3><p>Sun against water. Pick a plant.</p><svg width=\"720\" height=\"440\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Houseplants by sun and water\"><g><line x1=\"44\" x2=\"44\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"16\" /><text x=\"44\" y=\"418\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text></g><g><line x1=\"174.4\" x2=\"174.4\" y1=\"400\" y2=\"16\" /><text x=\"174.4\" y=\